{"slug":"march-blues","title":"March Blues","blurb":"a 12-bar blues in F from the U.S. Marine Band's \"The Washington Post\" (a 6/8 march) split into stems, with Army bugle calls answering in the second chorus. The same piece as march-blues.yaml, in Apricity's text language.","score":"examples/march-blues.apr","code":"# March Blues \u2014 a 12-bar blues in F from the U.S. Marine Band's \"The Washington Post\"\n# (a 6/8 march) split into stems, with Army bugle calls answering in the second chorus.\n# The same piece as march-blues.yaml, in Apricity's text language.\n\ntempo 100                 # one beat = the march's dotted-quarter pulse: 12/8 shuffle bars\nkey F mixolydian          # lets the dominant sevenths count as in-key\nsamples ../samples\n\nclip groove = marine-band/stems/WashingtonPost/drums.wav   pick 2bars  warp beats\nclip tuba   = marine-band/stems/WashingtonPost/bass.wav    pick 1bar\nclip horns  = marine-band/stems/WashingtonPost/other.wav   pick 1bar\nclip bugle  = citizen-dj/loc-jukebox-popular/Army-bugle-calls_jukebox-118367_001_00-00-56.wav  pick 1bar\n\n# chorus 1: quick change in bar 2, turnaround in bar 12\nchords I7 IV7 I7 .  | IV7 . I7 .  | V7 IV7 I7 V7\n# chorus 2\nchords I7 IV7 I7 .  | IV7 . I7 .  | V7 IV7 I7 .\n\ntrack groove  transpose 0  volume -3        # drums don't follow the chords\ntrack tuba    follow                      # oom-pah bass moved to each root: I\u2013IV\u2013V\ntrack horns   follow  bars 13-24  volume -2 # the riff, in parallel on every chord\ntrack bugle   at 15 19 23  volume -5        # call and response\n","provenance":[{"source":"groove","title":"The Washington Post \u2014 drums","kind":"clip","tracks":["groove"],"recordings":[{"title":"The Washington Post","part":"drums","composed":1889,"recorded":"2017","performer":"\"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band","credit":"\"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band, The Complete Marches of John Philip Sousa, Vol. 3.","rights":"Public domain (composition pre-1923; recording is a work of the U.S. Government).","licence":"Public domain","source_page":"https://www.marineband.marines.mil/Audio-Resources/The-Complete-Marches-of-John-Philip-Sousa/The-Washington-Post-March/","parts":["drums"]}]},{"source":"tuba","title":"The Washington Post \u2014 bass","kind":"clip","tracks":["tuba"],"recordings":[{"title":"The Washington Post","part":"bass","composed":1889,"recorded":"2017","performer":"\"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band","credit":"\"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band, The Complete Marches of John Philip Sousa, Vol. 3.","rights":"Public domain (composition pre-1923; recording is a work of the U.S. Government).","licence":"Public domain","source_page":"https://www.marineband.marines.mil/Audio-Resources/The-Complete-Marches-of-John-Philip-Sousa/The-Washington-Post-March/","parts":["bass"]}]},{"source":"horns","title":"The Washington Post \u2014 horns","kind":"clip","tracks":["horns"],"recordings":[{"title":"The Washington Post","part":"horns","composed":1889,"recorded":"2017","performer":"\"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band","credit":"\"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band, The Complete Marches of John Philip Sousa, Vol. 3.","rights":"Public domain (composition pre-1923; recording is a work of the U.S. Government).","licence":"Public domain","source_page":"https://www.marineband.marines.mil/Audio-Resources/The-Complete-Marches-of-John-Philip-Sousa/The-Washington-Post-March/","parts":["horns"]}]},{"source":"bugle","title":"Army bugle calls","kind":"clip","tracks":["bugle"],"recordings":[{"title":"Army bugle calls","part":null,"composed":null,"recorded":null,"performer":null,"credit":"Citizen DJ Project, Library of Congress, National Jukebox.","rights":"Public domain (published before 1923; Music Modernization Act).","licence":"Public domain","source_page":"https://citizen-dj.labs.loc.gov/loc-jukebox-popular/use/","parts":[]}]}],"captions":{},"audio":{"sources":["breakdow